{"availability":"available","full":"MichaelAyles/kicad-library","name":"kicad-library","description":"CircuitSnips.com - open source hardware repository","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":30,"forks":0,"created":"2025-10-16T19:02:52Z","updated":"2026-10-08T12:14:50Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.circuitsnips.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://circuitsnips.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:24.202Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:24.202Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:24.202Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:44:24.202Z","stars":30,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CircuitSnips is a community-driven platform for sharing and discovering KiCad subcircuits. A place where engineers can share their proven circuit designs and help others avoid reinventing the wheel.","The comparison to Thingiverse is deliberate: this is for side projects and quick prototypes, not production designs. If you want to throw an ESP on a board with an AMS1117 and an MCP2515 for a weekend project, these circuits are a reasonable starting point. You should always check everything yourself, but if you're repeatedly throwing boards together with the same jellybean parts, why not have a library to pull from?","Copy circuit in KiCad → Paste on CircuitSnips → Someone else searches → Copies to their project. That's it."],"features":["Interactive schematic preview using KiCanvas (WebGL viewer)","Copy to clipboard with embedded attribution (author, source, license)","GitHub OAuth and email/password authentication","8 open hardware licenses (CERN-OHL-S-2.0, MIT, Apache-2.0, GPL-3.0, etc.)","Weighted full-text search (prioritizes tags > title > description)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MichaelAyles/kicad-library/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eefb263ddbfb3f52b66c1183bc1f73a02b5f929fd639b6d9b3d5246cff1fa273","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:24.286Z"},"overviewChec